--TEST--
`Core\Router\Match::accessAs<E>` answers a case of `E`, so a class whose constant a route's `allow:` names is refused as its type argument, and so is a scalar — `rule:security/access-is-checked-for-presence-not-meaning`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Router\Match::accessAs
namespace App;

class Policy
{
    public const string STAFF = "staff";
}

?Core\Router\Match $match = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/");
if ($match != null) {
    echo $match->accessAs<Policy>() == null ? "none" : "some", "\n";
    echo $match->accessAs<int>() == null ? "none" : "some", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0841]: `Core\Router\Match::accessAs` returns a case of an enum, and `App\Policy` is not an enum
   --> case.nvs:12:27
%A
error[E0841]: `Core\Router\Match::accessAs` returns a case of an enum, and `int` is not an enum
   --> case.nvs:13:27
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
